node_modules/
build/
dist/
# Test-coverage REPORTS only. This was an unanchored `coverage/`, which matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth — and so silently excluded the public
# /coverage/ archive route added in Stage 06-R. Committing would have dropped
# app/(public)/coverage/page.tsx from the repository and broken the build on a
# clean checkout. Anchored to where vitest actually writes reports instead.
/coverage/
/apps/web/coverage/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env*
!.env.example
!.env.staging.example

# Project documentation and per-stage reports live OUTSIDE this repository,
# in ../NFRGUIDE Document, by the owner's decision: they are a record of how the
# work was done, not part of what gets deployed, and they were making the
# published repository mostly prose. README.md stays, because it is the first
# thing anyone opening the repository reads.
/docs/
/*.md
!/README.md
